Wiz's ChaosDB disclosure and its technical walkthrough are the research the page reconstructs. Wiz's original announcement and its discovery and protection guidance are two more Wiz posts the page lists. Wiz's PEACH tenant isolation framework is the one the page names in stage 01 and in its vendor assessment defense.

The MSRC post is Microsoft's own update on the vulnerability, the advisory the page's disclosure says is cited alongside the Wiz research. The MITRE page defines T1611, Escape to Host, the technique the page maps to stage 02.

Say the disclosure aloud once more: this reconstruction is sourced to research published by Wiz, and the site's author works at Wiz. Caveat the trust you grant accordingly.

